==Old English==
===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/æɑrm/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology 1===
{{proto|Germanic|arma-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|armo-|lang=ang}}, from ''*ar-, *arə-'' ‘fit, join’.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|arm}}, Old Saxon {{term|arm}} (Dutch {{term|arm|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|arm}} (German {{term|Arm}}), Old Norse {{term|armr}} (Swedish {{term|arm|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌰𐍂𐌼𐍃}}.  The PIE root is also the source of Old Church Slavonic {{term|рамо}} (Russian {{term|рамо||shoulder}}), Latin {{term|armus}}.

